# Everything the pipeline produces. All of it is re-fetchable from OpenStreetMap
# and the Environment Agency, so none of it is committed -- run sources/run.sh.
#   data/raw/       Overpass extract + LIDAR GeoTIFFs as downloaded
#   data/interim/   VRT mosaics and intermediate arrays
#   data/derived/   margate.gpkg
#   data/out/       tiled roads, massing, coast splats, terrain heightmaps
data/

.DS_Store

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Throwaway site configs written by sources/tests/dryrun.py
sources/config/sites/_*.json

# Unreal Engine build products under projects/ (the source of truth is text: .uproject, Source/, Config/,
# Plugins/*/Source, and the scripts under Tools/ that regenerate Content). Never commit these.
projects/*/Binaries/
projects/*/Intermediate/
projects/*/Saved/
projects/*/DerivedDataCache/
projects/*/Build/
projects/*/.vs/
projects/*/.vsconfig
projects/*/*.sln
projects/*/*.suo
projects/*/*.xcworkspace
projects/*/*.code-workspace
projects/*/Plugins/*/Binaries/
projects/*/Plugins/*/Intermediate/
# Blender prototype outputs (renders are committed deliberately via LFS from Tools/blender/renders only)
projects/*/Tools/blender/out/
*.blend1

# Unreal Content/ is entirely generated: projects/one/Tools/ue/01_bootstrap.py builds the map,
# materials and profile assets (~1 min), and 02/03/06 import the landscape, streetscape and massing
# from data/<site>/out/unreal/ (gigabytes once the landscape lands). The scripts are the source of
# truth -- a fresh clone runs them rather than checking out a derivative that goes stale silently.
projects/one/Content/

# The photo warchest (sources/fetch/photos.py) and the open geodata that frames it
# (sources/fetch/geo.py). Both are re-fetchable from public endpoints, and images/ runs to
# tens of GB at full resolution, so neither is committed -- same rule as data/. The source of
# truth is the two fetchers plus sources/config/thanet_towns.json.
#   images/_catalogue/  what each source holds over Thanet (regenerate: photos.py catalogue)
#   images/<town>/      the image files and their MANIFEST.jsonl
#   geo/                OSM, Historic England, Environment Agency and OS OpenData layers
# The READMEs are the exception: they are written by hand and describe how to rebuild the rest.
images/*
!images/README.md
geo/*
!geo/README.md

# Generated recovery work is preserved in dated, verified LFS archives under backups/.
# Source code lives in sources/ and projects/; consult output/README.md before restoring.
/output/*
!/output/README.md
